(RESERVE BANK OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(DEPARTMENT OF REGULATION, CENTRAL OFFICE, MUMBAI) Tj
T*
(RBI/2024-25/145 DOR.STR.REC.20/21.04.048/2024-25) Tj
T*
(September 27, 2024) Tj
T*
(Framework for Compromise Settlements and Technical Write-offs) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Board-Approved Policy: All commercial banks and NBFCs must implement comprehensive Board-approved policies laying down the) Tj
T*
(delegation of powers, eligibility criteria, and haircut rationales for undertaking compromise settlements and technical write-offs.) Tj
T*
(2. Wilful Defaulters and Fraud Accounts: Regulated entities may enter into compromise settlements with borrowers categorized as) Tj
T*
(wilful defaulters or fraud accounts without prejudice to any ongoing criminal proceedings. However, such settlements require the) Tj
T*
(specific prior approval of the Board of Directors of the bank or NBFC.) Tj
T*
(3. Cooling-off Period for Fresh Credit: In respect of borrowers where a compromise settlement has been finalized, a mandatory) Tj
T*
(cooling-off period of not less than 12 months shall apply before the RE can grant any fresh credit exposure. For restructuring,) Tj
T*
(the cooling period remains governed by prudential norms.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 809 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(4. Technical Write-offs: Technical write-offs are an accounting mechanism to clear non-performing assets from the balance sheet) Tj
T*
(without waiving the legal claims against the borrower. All technical write-offs must be approved by the Audit Committee of the Board \(ACB\)) Tj
T*
(and tracked in separate off-balance sheet recovery ledgers.) Tj
T*
(5. Reporting to Credit Bureaus: Every compromise settlement and technical write-off must be reported to all four licensed Credit) Tj
T*
(Information Companies \(CICs\), distinctly tagging the account status as 'Settled' or 'Written-Off' to ensure transparent credit reporting.) Tj
T*
(6. Compromise Terms: The settlement agreement must specify the down payment percentage, payment schedule, and default consequences.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 902 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(7. Valuation of Underlying Collateral: In all compromise proposals where the aggregate outstanding ledger balance exceeds) Tj
T*
(rupees one crore \(INR 1,00,00,000\), regulated entities must obtain at least two independent valuation reports from registered valuers) Tj
T*
(to establish current realizable market value of mortgaged properties.) Tj
T*
(8. Staff Accountability Examination: Every compromise settlement involving sacrifice of debt must be accompanied by a documented) Tj
T*
(examination of staff accountability. Any settlement where staff culpability or procedural malfeasance is suspected must be referred) Tj
T*
(to the bank's vigilance department.) Tj
T*
(9. Concession Authority: Concessions or waivers of interest and principal cannot be sanctioned by any authority who was associated with) Tj
T*
(the sanction of the original credit facility.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Length 756 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(10. Reporting to the Board: A quarterly review report of all compromise settlements and technical write-offs approved by various) Tj
T*
(delegated authorities must be submitted to the Board of Directors.) Tj
T*
(11. Public Disclosures: Banks and NBFCs shall disclose in their notes to accounts the total number of accounts settled, total outstanding) Tj
T*
(dues, amount of sacrifice or haircut, and recoveries effected through legal action.) Tj
T*
(12. Recovery Retention: Amounts recovered subsequent to technical write-offs must be credited directly to the profit and loss statement) Tj
T*
(under non-interest miscellaneous income.) Tj
T*
(Yours faithfully,) Tj
T*
(\(Rajeshwar Rao\)) Tj
T*
(Chief General Manager) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
